 S("雙篇：渡輪新航線報導＋更正來函", 300, [
  "Ferry Service to Link Port Ellis and Downtown\n\nHARBOR CITY (April 28) - Commuters from Port Ellis will soon have an alternative to the crowded Coastal Highway. Bayline Ferries will launch a weekday service between the Port Ellis marina and Harbor City's Pier 9 on Monday, May 4.\n\nTwo new vessels, each able to carry 180 passengers, will depart every 30 minutes between 6:00 and 9:00 A.M. and return between 4:00 and 7:30 P.M. Morning ferries will make a brief stop at Grant Pier, near the Harbor City Convention Center, before continuing to Pier 9. The trip will take about 35 minutes.\n\nA one-way ticket will cost $6.50, and a monthly pass will be available for $150. Passengers may bring bicycles on board for an additional $1 per trip.\n\n\"Every car we take off the highway helps,\" said Bayline chief executive Gloria Fuentes. \"We expect the service to ease congestion noticeably within its first year.\"\n\nTickets go on sale online on Friday, May 1.",
  "To the Editor:\n\nThank you for your April 28 article about our new Port Ellis commuter ferry. I would like to clarify two points so that your readers can plan their trips.\n\nFirst, the $150 figure you reported is the price of our Premier pass, which includes a reserved seat in the upper cabin. Our Standard monthly pass, which most commuters will want, costs $25 less.\n\nSecond, repairs to the dock at Grant Pier are taking longer than expected. Until the work is finished, which we expect to be in early July, all morning ferries will travel directly to Pier 9.\n\nIn addition, I am pleased to announce that, to celebrate the launch, bicycles will travel free of charge throughout the month of May.\n\nNathan Osei\nDirector of Communications, Bayline Ferries\nApril 30"], [
   ("What is the article mainly about?",
    ["The launch of a new commuter service", "The construction of a convention center", "Repairs planned for the Coastal Highway", "A change in leadership at a ferry firm"],
    "r-main",
    "報導主要在說 Bayline Ferries 5 月 4 日起開辦 Port Ellis 到市中心的平日通勤渡輪＝新通勤服務開辦。會展中心只是用來說明 Grant Pier 的位置；Coastal Highway 是被提到很擁擠，沒說要整修；執行長只是被引述，沒有人事異動。"),
   ("How much does a Standard monthly pass cost?",
    ["$125", "$150", "$175", "$6.50"],
    "r-multi",
    "雙篇整合：(1) 報導寫月票 $150；(2) 來函更正：$150 其實是含預留座位的 Premier 月票，一般的 Standard 月票便宜 $25 → $150 − $25＝$125。$150 是報導的舊資訊、實際上是 Premier 的價格；$175 是把 $25 加上去；$6.50 是單程票。"),
   ("What will passengers be unable to do during the first week of service?",
    ["Get off a morning ferry at Grant Pier", "Take a bicycle on board free of charge", "Buy their ferry tickets online", "Board a ferry in Port Ellis at 6:00 A.M."],
    "r-multi",
    "雙篇整合：(1) 報導說早班船會先停靠 Grant Pier 再開到 Pier 9；(2) 來函說 Grant Pier 碼頭整修延誤，預計七月初才完工，在那之前早班船直接開到 Pier 9＝5 月 4 日開航的第一週無法在 Grant Pier 下船。報導說自行車每趟加收 $1，但來函說整個五月自行車免費，舊資訊已被推翻；報導說 5 月 1 日開始網路售票；早班船從 6:00 開始每 30 分鐘一班。"),
   ("In the article, the word \"ease\" in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to",
    ["reduce", "comfort", "simplify", "slow"],
    "r-syn",
    "ease congestion＝減輕交通壅塞 → reduce。comfort 是「安慰」人，simplify 是「簡化」程序或說明，slow 是「使變慢」，都不能用在「___ 壅塞」上表達減輕的意思。"),
   ("What is NOT mentioned in the article about the ferries?",
    ["The food sold on board", "How many passengers each can carry", "How often they leave in the morning", "How long the trip to Pier 9 takes"],
    "r-not",
    "報導提到每艘船可載 180 人、早上每 30 分鐘一班、航程約 35 分鐘，唯一沒提到的是船上販售的餐點。"),
 ]),
